node-agent/tests/concurrent_start.rs, FakeVmm (the node agent's own locking is
what is under test, not the VMM), macOS dev machine.

Before -- everything except ResumeCat under the node-wide ops mutex:
  single launch 74 ms; 8 concurrent 539 ms; fully serialized would be 592 ms;
  speedup 1.10x

After -- per-Cat lock held unconditionally, node-wide lock only for launches that
allocate node-global state (kernel-NBD device allocation), concurrency bounded by
a separate launch ceiling:
  single launch 65-76 ms; 8 concurrent 113-137 ms; fully serialized would be
  520-608 ms; speedup 4.03x-5.33x

Also asserted: with a ceiling of 2, six concurrent launches all queue and
succeed, and a Cat whose memory exceeds the wake budget is still launchable --
launches are counted, not charged in resume-commitment bytes.
